---
// The row of panels under a commentary section's title: the paired lecture,
// and that section's teaching aid in its two formats. D47 sec 4 (the aid is
// reachable from its commentary section, beside the lecture) as specified by
// the Web Dev Ask of 20 Sep 2026 and the Editor's shape rulings of that date.
//
// The third panel of the triptych is the page this sits on. D47's reason is
// the Editor's: a reader who has one of the three is the reader most likely to
// want the other two.
//
// The aid is found from the collection by matching its `section` against this
// section's id — never from a hand-maintained list, which is the whole point
// of the data contract (D47 sec 4). Resolution happens in the route's
// getStaticPaths; this component only renders what it is handed.
//
// SHAPE. All frames are 16:9 and the same height, so the three thumbnails line
// up whatever their own proportions. The tall 9:16 is centred in its frame and
// padded with --color-bg — the page background, not the slide field — so it
// floats on the page rather than sitting in a visible box (the Editor's
// ruling, 20 Sep 2026).
//
// Each panel is ONE link wrapping its frames and its label, so the thumbnail
// and the words under it go to the same place and the label is the link's
// accessible name. The lecture's label reads "Watch the Lecture"; the aid's
// two images share the single label "Teaching Aids" — plural by the Editor's
// ruling of 20 Sep 2026, where D47 gives each pair ONE aid in two formats. The
// divergence is nominal and deliberate: a teacher sees two downloadable
// artifacts.
//
// IT DEGRADES RATHER THAN LEAVING A GAP (ask sec 9). Every published section
// must keep rendering: a section with a lecture and no aid shows one panel, a
// section with neither shows nothing at all and the row does not appear.
// Twenty-odd published sections are in the first case today and stay there
// until the D47 sec 6 migration reaches them.
import { slideAssetUrl, slideUrl, lectureUrl, lectureThumbUrl } from '../lib/site';

interface Props {
  sectionId: string;
  /** True when the paired lecture is published AND its thumbnail file exists. */
  showLecture: boolean;
  /** The section's teaching aid, already visibility-checked, or null. */
  aid: any | null;
}
const { sectionId, showLecture, aid } = Astro.props;
const aidAlt = aid ? (aid.data.imageAlt ?? `Projectable slide: ${aid.data.title}`) : '';
---
{(showLecture || aid) && (
  <nav class="triptych" aria-label="Lecture and teaching aid for this section">
    {showLecture && (
      <a class="triptych__panel" href={lectureUrl(sectionId)}>
        <span class="triptych__frames">
          <span class="triptych__frame">
            <img src={lectureThumbUrl(sectionId)} alt="" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" />
          </span>
        </span>
        <span class="triptych__label">Watch the Lecture</span>
      </a>
    )}

    {aid && (
      <a class="triptych__panel" href={slideUrl(aid.id)}>
        <span class="triptych__frames">
          <span class="triptych__frame">
            <img src={slideAssetUrl(aid.id, '16x9')} alt={aidAlt} width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" />
          </span>
          <span class="triptych__frame triptych__frame--tall">
            <img src={slideAssetUrl(aid.id, '9x16')} alt="" width="1080" height="1920" loading="lazy" />
          </span>
        </span>
        <span class="triptych__label">Teaching Aids</span>
      </a>
    )}
  </nav>
)}
